WEBVTT

NOTE
English summary of the on-screen text and visual sequence; not a structural specification.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Jefferson in Athens: installation animation. Illustrative guidance.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Proposed finished setting. Sculpture: 100 cm high. Overall height: approximately 220 cm.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Overview of the proposed method. Cost, timing and site details require confirmation; see current project status.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Excavate and position the reinforcement grid. The engineer determines footing dimensions, depth and reinforcement.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Set vertical reinforcement and pour the footing. Final reinforcement and concrete specification require engineering confirmation.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Position and brace the formwork, then pour the cylinder. Proposed constructed height above grade: 130 cm.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Allow the concrete to gain strength. Remove formwork, finish the surface, prime and paint. Backfill to grade.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Install the sculpture. Confirm orientation and the site-specific attachment method with the studio and engineer.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Illustration of threaded-rod attachment and seating of the sculpture. The upper 10 cm of the base fits into its underside recess.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:38.580
Complete the planted setting. Landscaping and the final base finish remain subject to confirmation.

